## Summary
The GDPR has imposed over €114 million in fines on companies like Google and Facebook within its first 20 months of implementation. Regulators are expected to propose changes in 2020 to adapt to evolving data privacy challenges. The article highlights the ongoing enforcement and potential updates to the regulation.

## Key Points
- GDPR regulators issued hundreds of fines totaling more than €114 million in the first 20 months.
- Major companies such as Google and Facebook have been penalized under GDPR.
- Changes to GDPR are anticipated to be proposed in 2020.
- Enforcement actions emphasize the importance of compliance with data protection laws.
- The regulation is expected to evolve with new modifications in response to emerging issues.


